    "body": "Construct two actual native Word RAM suppliers from the frozen PR #4610 round-three word: a kernel-153 quotient and its orthogonal-restriction counterpart. They have complementary explicit B/C interfaces on the same 56 exceptional ports. The restriction includes all four required paid warp repairs. Its complete paid moment improves strictly over its predecessor for every exponent 0 ≤ t < 1, with unchanged independent helper profile. This does not establish a new multiplication κ: no profitable complete controller was found.\r\n\r\nThe package includes all-width free-group/operator proofs, explicit mixed-controller routing and endpoint-gauge lemmas, exact phase-aware native artifacts and a standard-library-only isolated replay. It checks both 632-row formal endpoints, 72 shared maps, 180 warp classes in both orientations, all typed main normalizers, and 2088 quotient / 2048 restriction frame pairs in both orientations. Payloads regenerate exactly; optimized source-corruption controls must reject drift. No Lean formalization or Linux replay of this new package is claimed.\r\n\r\nCredit Cao Yifan's #4610 native word, DaysSky's quotient route, Dugongue's #4654 construction, Cinna Davis and the PR589/PR4470 supplier/controller lineage, Nick Petalas, Ryanson Jonathan, Rohan Arun, zxv, Jacob Alan Sussman, and retained source authors. Concurrent #4655/#4658/#4659/#4660/#4665 address related scoped questions; #4660's B extraction is not claimed as new here. The latest #4610 compiler tightening is acknowledged and is not exceeded. Prepared for Dugongue with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, using one coordinating worker and three parallel workers.\r\n\r\nRemaining obligation before any exponent improvement: a profitable complete consumer for these actual typed interfaces, followed by finite-reserve compiler and outer-transfer admission. Canonical main and the selected frontier are unchanged.\r\n",
    "title": "Construct complementary native suppliers with a strict local moment improvement (no new kappa)",
